      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A wingless, dragon-like tyrannosaur with knobbly hide, shimmering scales along its back, vestigial forearms, and a spine-lined tail."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Senses",
          "lines": [
            "Blindsight 30 ft."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Skills",
          "lines": [
            "Perception +4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Damage immunities",
          "lines": [
            "Acid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Base creature",
          "lines": [
            "Tyrannosaurus Rex"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Attacks",
          "lines": [
            "Bite · Melee Weapon Attack · +10 to hit · reach 10 ft. · 4d12 + 7 piercing",
            "Tail · Melee Weapon Attack · +10 to hit · reach 10 ft. · 3d8 + 7 bludgeoning"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Traits mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Queen of Thieves' champion · The Queen of Thieves has permanently charmed Big Linda. Linda usually follows the Queen's spoken orders and emerges from her Court of Thieves arena den when the Queen whistles."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Actions mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Multiattack · 2 attacks · One Bite and one Tail attack, each against a different target.",
            "Bite · +10 to hit · reach 10 ft. · One target takes 33 (4d12 + 7) piercing damage on a hit. A Medium or smaller creature is grappled (escape DC 17) and restrained until that grapple ends. During the grapple Linda cannot bite another target. · 4d12 + 7 piercing",
            "Tail · +10 to hit · reach 10 ft. · One target takes 20 (3d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage on a hit. · 3d8 + 7 bludgeoning",
            "Acid Spew · Recharge 5–6 · Creatures in a 30-ft. cone take the printed 49 (11d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success. · DC 15 Dexterity · 11d8 acid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Dungeons of Drakkenheim, p. 163, applies these changes to the 2014 Tyrannosaurus Rex. The base block is available in SRD 5.1, p. 279.",
            "The adventure gives the variant CR 9. It does not print an XP value."
          ]
        }
      ],
